# Web-design-skills stack (not Impeccable)

When the user is working on a **client landing / local business site** (Instagram/Maps discovery, brand direction, fonts/colors, brand kit, build, QA) — including names like Mesal, Baterías, or “nuevo cliente” — use the **web-design-skills** stack:

`web-discovery` → `visual-direction` → `brand-kit-gen` → `landing-build` (+ `landing-craft`) → `landing-qa`

Guide: `docs/web-design-skills/PIPELINE.md`  
Client briefs live only under `docs/web-design-skills/clients/<slug>/`.

## Hard rules

1. **Do not use Impeccable** for this pipeline unless the user explicitly says `/impeccable` or “usá Impeccable”.
2. **Do not treat root `PRODUCT.md` / `DESIGN.md` as the current client.** Those may belong to another project (e.g. Baterías CABA). For Mesal (or any new client), only read `docs/web-design-skills/clients/<slug>/`.
3. After discovery is confirmed, the next skill is **`visual-direction`** (`.cursor/skills/visual-direction/`), **not** Impeccable `new-work` / concept-seed / decision page.
4. Brand kits use **`brand-kit-gen`** + OpenRouter — not Higgsfield / Impeccable visualize — unless the user asks otherwise.
5. **Build default is Astro** (+ CSS variables from `direction.md`) under `docs/web-design-skills/clients/<slug>/site/`. Do not default to raw `index.html` unless the user waives Astro.
6. For psychology-law correction of an existing page, use **`laws-of-ux-correct`** (code + visual). Do not confuse it with Impeccable critique.

If unsure which stack: ask once — “¿Seguimos con web-design-skills o con Impeccable?” — default answer for client landings is **web-design-skills**.
